Choose a fluid model when several physical mechanisms compete (@fd-interfaces-review: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @fluid-dynamics, #source "../sources/Fundamentals-of-Multiphase-Flow-Brennen.lingua#r_0T6RH2YC70Z23SR3H4QZDJ69JM", #source "../sources/Non-Newtonian-Fluid-Dynamics-Hinch.lingua#r_06KY7WE9WYAF856YQKQXHY1DS3", #source "../sources/Microfluidic-Physics-Squires-Quake.lingua#r_5TN8JGKY1B6VKGJQG859J61JE2", #source "../sources/CFD-Verification-and-Validation-NPARC.lingua#r_7P72ZWZEJ0SVMWFDGK52N9AZPV", #fluid-dynamics "../../../../inquiry/metrology/applications/Mass-volume-and-flow.lingua#r_7S09P54V6ADP28CA0FTZ6SMHQZ") { r_43864KY2VCBNKWX8VEGNPA2HCR
**Read:** [Fundamentals of Multiphase Flow — Christopher E. Brennen](../sources/Fundamentals-of-Multiphase-Flow-Brennen.lingua#r_0T6RH2YC70Z23SR3H4QZDJ69JM), model hierarchy and closure discussions; [Lectures on Non-Newtonian Fluid Dynamics — John Hinch](../sources/Non-Newtonian-Fluid-Dynamics-Hinch.lingua#r_06KY7WE9WYAF856YQKQXHY1DS3), constitutive modelling and experiments; [Microfluidics: Fluid physics at the nanoliter scale — Squires and Quake](../sources/Microfluidic-Physics-Squires-Quake.lingua#r_5TN8JGKY1B6VKGJQG859J61JE2), comparisons across physical mechanisms; [CFD verification and validation — NPARC Alliance](../sources/CFD-Verification-and-Validation-NPARC.lingua#r_7P72ZWZEJ0SVMWFDGK52N9AZPV), separation of numerical and physical evidence.

Take a system with at least three competing mechanisms: a particle-laden coating, a heated microchannel, a bubbly line or a compliant pulsatile passage. Identify observable quantities and the purpose of the prediction before choosing a model family. Build a scale table with measured or traceable input ranges.

Derive a hierarchy of models from a common set of balances. State what each retains, averages or neglects; include constitutive and interface conditions. Predict a regime boundary where a simpler model should fail and design a comparison that can reveal that failure. Do not tune all models against the same one observable and call the result validation.

Defend the resulting model using independent evidence, conservation checks, numerical convergence where applicable and an uncertainty account. Explain what remains unidentified and which additional observation would matter most. This reasoning connects the advanced mechanisms to the later computational, experimental and service investigations.

